const appendices = [
  H1("Appendix A. Adapters for the official schedulers"),
  P("CaWoSched (KIT-EAE/CaWoSched, commit dfc8e49) and CWM (KIT-EAE/CWM, commit 50e9ef5) were built from source. CWM needed two non-algorithmic changes: read-only accessors that print the final schedule, and a missing standard-library include for GCC 13. CaWoSched's validity check rejects edges without data, so every cross-machine edge carries a one-minute transfer inside CaWoSched; this makes its plans slightly conservative in our transfer-free simulator. Intensity over the windows up to D is inverted and rescaled to a budget between the total idle power and the idle power plus frac × the dynamic power. On development data (five workflows, two targets, six submissions, two deadline factors; n = 120 per cell) the full range (frac = 1.0) gave CaWoSched an oracle emission saving of 4.85%, against 2.34–2.56% for frac 0.2–0.4. On the heterogeneous platform (development data, raw CWM) frac 1.0 gave −0.1% against −1.4% to −1.9%. Every schedule returned by either tool was checked for precedence, capacity and the deadline."),
  H1("Appendix B. Heterogeneous platform"),
  P("With machines m of busy power p(m), idle power p₀(m) and speed v(m), a task of work w runs ⌈w / v(m)⌉ minutes. All machines stay on until W = max(D, makespan), so emissions are Σᵢ (p(mᵢ) − p₀(mᵢ)) ∫ I dt over each task plus Σₘ p₀(m) ∫₀ᵂ I dt. The second term is the same for all plans that finish by D, so schedulers optimise the marginal (busy − idle) cost. HEFT ranks tasks by upward rank with mean durations and places each on the machine with the earliest finish time, with insertion. CA-List and CA-LS consider all machines and start times; the gate's risk term is scaled by the larger of the two task energies."),
  H1("Appendix C. Deviations from the sealed plans"),
  P("(1) Main study: the scheduler horizon was extended to D + T and the planning signal padded with its last value, because intermediate attempts inside the deadline repair could place tasks beyond the 47-h vintage before being rejected; valid plans never use the padded values. The partial output of the failed launch was deleted unread. (2) Main study: the run was split by seed to fit a two-hour process limit; the design is unchanged. (3) Main study: the CaWoSched adapter's documentation wrongly said its budget mapping followed CWM's; the code was unchanged, and Appendix A states the mapping used. (4) Platform study: CaWoSched was added as an exploratory analysis after the results, because the reason for excluding it was wrong (Section 5.5)."),
];

